<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?><?xml-stylesheet href="http://www.blogger.com/styles/atom.css" type="text/css"?><feed xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom' xmlns:openSearch='http://a9.com/-/spec/opensearchrss/1.0/' xmlns:gd="http://schemas.google.com/g/2005"><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post115636719773741673..comments</id><updated>2017-04-13T04:47:21.148-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Comments on Pro Libertate: The Madness That Is &quot;War Patriotism&quot;</title><link rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#feed' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/feeds/comments/default'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html'/><link rel="hub" href="http://pubsubhubbub.appspot.com/"/><author><name>William N. Grigg</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/14368220509514750246</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='32' height='19' src='http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-5rhFUXs_62I/VgVL2E3rMII/AAAAAAAAMJ4/cjJOyI7W208/s220/Photo%2BRon%2BPaul%2BLiberty%2BReport.jpg'/></author><generator version='7.00' uri='http://www.blogger.com'>Blogger</generator><openSearch:totalResults>13</openSearch:totalResults><openSearch:startIndex>1</openSearch:startIndex><openSearch:itemsPerPage>25</openSearch:itemsPerPage><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115685814231046748</id><published>2006-08-29T07:29:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-29T07:29:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Rick wrote:being in the military, if i went out an...</title><content type='html'>Rick wrote:being in the military, if i went out and condemned the sins that are going on at the national level, i will find myself in prison and unable to do what it is that the Lord has for me to do where i&#39;m at. there was an airforce general that did this long ago in criticizing clinton. what he said was 100% correct, but look what happened to him? why do most generals criticize policy after they get out? because they are muzzled from doing so while they are in the military because their actions will be construed as a UCMJ offense--contempt for officials.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; You are great, Thank You for serving; I only wish it was under better circumstances. Your right you can&#39;t speak out. One takes their Citizen hat off to put on their military hat. I as a Citizen, I speak out all the time for truth, justice, and a restored righteous American way; Even to the point of stating that judgement must fall on the head of baby Bush althought I always make it clear that he should be brought to justice through the proper chanels {Tried for Treason} and then executed.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Rick wrote:well, God told me to stay silent in my field. i got all this info, but i got to sit on it for now, and make use of it at a later date. that&#39;s what i&#39;ve been told to do.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Point well taken</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115685814231046748'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115685814231046748'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156858140000#c115685814231046748' title=''/><author><name>CHRISTOPHER</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/15761959164602925743</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-557695929"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 29, 2006 at 7:29 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115685694949764632</id><published>2006-08-29T07:09:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-29T07:09:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Rick wrote:chris,thanks for your comment. but coul...</title><content type='html'>Rick wrote:chris,&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;thanks for your comment. but could you provide me with the scripture where the Lord told john to criticize herod? i&#39;m interested.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;No particular scripture, The four Gospel accounts depict the whole thing, as you well know. A prophet has a wide range of actions that he, within his own will, can do&gt; all within the will of God.  &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Rick wrote: again, i make this point because i still think i&#39;ve not made myself clear. there is a time for silence, and there is a time to speak out. we cannot look at a group&#39;s silence as a sign that they condone evil, ie: the state of this nation. one never knows what God has told a group.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;Yes, still in general God now commands that ever United States Citizen get involved, speak out, do whatever is necessary to stop the satanic new world order this supercedes all else with the possible exception of preaching the Gospel.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115685694949764632'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115685694949764632'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156856940000#c115685694949764632' title=''/><author><name>CHRISTOPHER</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/15761959164602925743</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-557695929"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 29, 2006 at 7:09 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115653776949030001</id><published>2006-08-25T14:29:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-25T14:29:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>chris,thanks for your comment.  but could you prov...</title><content type='html'>chris,&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;thanks for your comment.  but could you provide me with the scripture where the Lord told john to criticize herod?  i&#39;m interested.  &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;again, i make this point because i still think i&#39;ve not made myself clear.  there is a time for silence, and there is a time to speak out.  we cannot look at a group&#39;s silence as a sign that they condone evil, ie: the state of this nation.  one never knows what God has told a group.    &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;being in the military, if i went out and condemned the sins that are going on at the national level, i will find myself in prison and unable to do what it is that the Lord has for me to do where i&#39;m at.  there was an airforce general that did this long ago in criticizing clinton.  what he said was 100% correct, but look what happened to him?  why do most generals criticize policy after they get out?  because they are muzzled from doing so while they are in the military because their actions will be construed as a UCMJ offense--contempt for officials.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;well, God told me to stay silent in my field.  i got all this info, but i got to sit on it for now, and make use of it at a later date.  that&#39;s what i&#39;ve been told to do.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;and with that i must go run my errands.&lt;BR/&gt;take care all.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115653776949030001'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115653776949030001'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156537740000#c115653776949030001' title=''/><author><name>rick</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/12473173027048173880</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-870704727"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 25, 2006 at 2:29 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115652534729094486</id><published>2006-08-25T11:02:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-25T11:02:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Excellent! Dixie Dog, how you set Rick straight. O...</title><content type='html'>Excellent! Dixie Dog, how you set Rick straight. One more thing on John, Rick. The Baptist didn&#39;t get diverted; God directed him to do just as he did. John was the last of the Old Testament Prophets and came to his end just as God had ordained, he couldn&#39;t have become an Apostle. Remember how the Lord spoke of him ~&quot;Of the Old Testament there is none greater, yet the least in the Kingdom is greater than he&quot;</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115652534729094486'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115652534729094486'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156525320000#c115652534729094486' title=''/><author><name>CHRISTOPHER</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/15761959164602925743</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-557695929"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 25, 2006 at 11:02 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115652359960066017</id><published>2006-08-25T10:33:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-25T10:33:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Rick had commented on Church, State, and God&#39;s pur...</title><content type='html'>Rick had commented on Church, State, and God&#39;s purpose. It is God&#39;s will that every American be involved with preserving and improving our Nation. Pray about it Rick, He will confirm.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Rick, A Christian&#39;s Eternal Life is not based on fulfilling a purpose or any thing we do, only on what Jesus did. Rewards are based on our works.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;No Rick, God is not worried about our Nation, He is directing US all to do what ever WE can to stop the Satanic New World Order.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115652359960066017'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115652359960066017'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156523580000#c115652359960066017' title=''/><author><name>CHRISTOPHER</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/15761959164602925743</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-557695929"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 25, 2006 at 10:33 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115652280990516666</id><published>2006-08-25T10:20:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-25T10:20:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'></title><content type='html'>This comment has been removed by a blog administrator.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115652280990516666'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115652280990516666'/><author><name>CHRISTOPHER</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/15761959164602925743</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name='blogger.contentRemoved' value='true'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-557695929"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 25, 2006 at 10:20 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115651130096710724</id><published>2006-08-25T07:08:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-25T07:08:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Well, I took your comments in stride, but yes, sin...</title><content type='html'>Well, I took your comments in stride, but yes, since much of your commentary focused upon &quot;silence&quot; and the wisdom of it and the fact that Grigg mentioned nothing of it, that you were naturally speaking to me. But, if I was wrong, I apologize. I&#39;m not one to make a mountain out of a mole hill. Macht nichts.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Anyhow, I do have a simple question, ready? Should one do &lt;I&gt;everything&lt;/I&gt; an authority figure commands (or asks, matters not) of him/her, knowing that to disobey means his/hers probable demise even if the commands in question are unequivocal violations of the Word of God?&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;The simple answer to that question speaks volumes. Nevertheless, as you said, to each his own. But, may no one win the whole world, yet lose his soul in the end.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Regards ;).</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115651130096710724'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115651130096710724'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156511280000#c115651130096710724' title=''/><author><name>dixiedog</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/09845646940134894119</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-504942784"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 25, 2006 at 7:08 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115650612580140152</id><published>2006-08-25T05:42:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-25T05:42:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>DD,i think you took what i said to be aimed at you...</title><content type='html'>DD,&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;i think you took what i said to be aimed at you.  in no way was that my intent.  sounds like you took it as such.  i was speaking to the issue, not at you.  but a few points...my time is short.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;keeping silent:  there is a season for everything.  the japanese say that the nail that sticks up gets hammered down.  in foxe&#39;s book of matyrs, there is a story of a prince who despised what the catholic leaders were doing.  so instead of waiting till he was king and then dealing with them, he spoke out against them and told them what he would do to them once he was king.  well, they convinced his father to kill him and he was executed.  he should have stayed quiet.  joseph got thrown in a pit for not keeping quiet.  even his father rebuked him.  he didn&#39;t have to say a word, but he went about bragging.  sometimes one must speak out, and at other times one must keep quiet.  after all, only a fool would criticize a king when he&#39;s in power.  gotta be careful between what&#39;s coming from the flesh and what&#39;s coming from God.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;spies:  spies aren&#39;t bad.  moses sent 12 of them in canaan.  i believe 2 were sent into jericho.  if you&#39;re not using spies, then you can bet that your enemy is...and he will defeat you because he now has the element of surprise and knows your plan.   &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;hey, to each his own.  i&#39;m going with what works for me...and what i&#39;ve written has gotten me where i am today.  but if i become a &quot;nail&quot;--before my time--i will be hammered down.  subtlety goes a long ways.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115650612580140152'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115650612580140152'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156506120000#c115650612580140152' title=''/><author><name>rick</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/12473173027048173880</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-870704727"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 25, 2006 at 5:42 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115648748069726689</id><published>2006-08-25T00:31:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-25T00:31:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>and to dixiedog, it may be a good thing that some ...</title><content type='html'>&lt;I&gt;and to dixiedog, it may be a good thing that some do not speak out against the horrors that are going on. hear me out. God has given everyone a purpose. each person is to walk in his purpose and accomplish it. to fail to do so would be to get to heaven and to hear....,&quot;I never knew you.&quot;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Hmm, no. You&#39;re confusing the judgement of rewards, in which Jesus would never say, &lt;A HREF=&quot;http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew%207:20-23;&amp;version=9;&quot; REL=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;&quot;I never knew you. Depart from me, ye that work iniquity.&quot;&lt;/A&gt;, with the final judgement (of the condemned) in which he would. Otherwise, how could you be in heaven in the first place, only to be cast out of the same?? If He &quot;never knew you&quot; you&#39;re not going to be present in Heaven. Remember the &quot;I&#39;ll never leave you or forsake you&quot; promise? But I digress.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;The &lt;A HREF=&quot;http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Revelations%2020:11-15;&amp;version=31;&quot; REL=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Great White Throne judgement&lt;/A&gt;, or final judgement, takes place after the millenial reign of Christ on earth. The judgement of rewards is for believers after they have been &lt;A HREF=&quot;http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?book_id=59&amp;chapter=4&amp;verse=17&amp;version=31&amp;context=verse&quot; REL=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;caught up together&lt;/A&gt; in the clouds with the ressurected dead in Christ to forever be with Christ in heaven.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;On a side note, I&#39;m absolutely not the caracature that you apparently have conjured up in your mind that I am. First, let me say that there&#39;s a difference between &lt;I&gt;tact&lt;/I&gt; and thereby keeping your mouth SHUT, unless it is profitable and edifying, and supporting evil &lt;I&gt;in your midst&lt;/I&gt; by keeping ones mouth SHUT. A huge difference. A roar is not always bad, if it&#39;s supportive of something good and righteous!&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;I don&#39;t want to get into a debate on theological nuances here, however, since they can distract from the core focus of the topic at hand ;). But, here we go...&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;I&gt;i seriously believe that, although the Lord does care about what&#39;s going on down here, He is not worried about it cuz He&#39;s got it under control. His message to the church right now may not be to focus on what our govt is doing because there are greater issues He needs to address in His church. i mean, if His church is focused on the affairs of this world, then how can it be effective spiritually if it&#39;s paying attention to man and not to God?&lt;/I&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Indeed, I believe most of that &lt;I&gt;in essence&lt;/I&gt; also. But you also bring to the forefront here yet another faux dichotomy. That is that those who are &quot;focused on the affairs of this world&quot; are simultaneously not focused on the spiritual affairs and condition of this world. That&#39;s just not so, or shouldn&#39;t be so. Let&#39;s again, look at what the Bible says about just this topic. Read &lt;A HREF=&quot;http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=james%202:15-16;&amp;version=9;&quot; REL=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;James 2:15-16&lt;/A&gt; for the most precise cut to the chase contrarian concept of what I think you&#39;re espousing here. Remember, that focus on God does not mean the matters of the world are left forlorn in the process. No, au contraire in fact! Also remember, there&#39;s no such thing as &quot;separation of church and state&quot; nonsense either, which seems at first glance to be part and parcel of your mantra here as well.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;I&gt;john the baptist had a mission--make way the coming of the Lord. now, along the way john got into doing something else...telling king herod he was wrong. herod was wrong, but what did God tell john to do? &quot;make way the coming of the Lord.&quot; what was his focus to be? God would send nathan to rebuke king david without many present, or in private, but john? john railed against herod in public. do we aever read &quot;and God sent john to see herod&quot;? nope. john got distracted from his focus/mission, and john got his head lopped off. when you think about it, had john not attacked herod, he may have become an apostle...but....he spoke to an issue that was not his purpose....and died because of it. (maybe i&#39;m wrong, but go tell the president at the white house gates he&#39;s x, y, and z and see what happens...hard to be affective for Christ behind bars). but i digress. back to my point.&lt;/I&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Rick. It doesn&#39;t matter that he, as you say, &quot;railed&quot; against Herod, since many all through history were decapitated &lt;I&gt;anyway&lt;/I&gt; because they didn&#39;t RAIL AGAINST CHRIST or RAIL FOR whatever pet philosophy the leader in question harbored. You can be loudly silent or loudly rail and still get slaughtered because you failed to either RAIL for/against or be SILENT for/against the proper philosophy in vogue at the time. Get it? That&#39;s just a fact of life (or of death as the case may be) we all have to contend with. You&#39;re certainly not saying that Christians should merely &quot;go along to get along&quot; are ya? That never works and, more significantly shows your true colors. Don&#39;t worry so much about dying, Rick, because it&#39;s coming one way or another. Just make sure that you&#39;re fighting the good fight of faith, regardless of when/how you die.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;I&gt;esther. esther had a purpose, one single purpose. save her people. had she done anything else the jews might have been wiped out. but of course that would not have happened because of God&#39;s promise, but things would have been in a bind. back to esther.&lt;/I&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Yes, Esther had a purpose. So did Joshua when he killed ALL the Amorites, with God&#39;s hand in it as well! We don&#39;t propose committing genocide today do we? Much of the OT was of such a savage nature for the simple reason that God had to make certain that the Israelites remained pure and did not mix with the heathen and pagan cultures and societies surrounding them ALL for the specific purpose of preserving the lineage through the subsequent centuries to the birth of Jesus. But Joshua did not simply kill all the heathen societies he confronted outright. It was only when/if they refused to bond with Israel and become their servants. Only &lt;I&gt;then&lt;/I&gt; were they to be slaughtered in their entirety.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;I&gt;ESTHER HAD TO KEEP HER MOUTH SHUT. satan knew God would try to save His people but did not know how He would do it. satan was expecting God to move one way, but did not see that He would sneak a jewess into the kings harem and have this jewess becaome his wife only so at the right moment, she would speak up to influence the king&#39;s decision. i&#39;m sure satan thought God was gonna replace the king or something.&lt;/I&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Same with Esther, but in a different manner of course, as she was likewise a key individual to maintaining the purpose of &lt;I&gt;preserving the the Jews at large, the lineage to Jesus&lt;/I&gt;.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;I&gt;so what am i saying? God has spies. and spies (like us) do not/should not reveal themselves until it&#39;s time to move or act. some groups may be quiet out of fear, but there are some, i am sure, that are spies, and are accomplishing a mission, that in the end, will change things. we want to see changes one way. and that &quot;way&quot; is what satan may be focused on and trying to prevent...and doing a good job at preventing. so God says, &quot;ok, i see you satan...and what you are doing. but while you are looking that way, I will move in these ways.&quot; it&#39;s not hard for God to trick satan. He did it at calvary. so if we are working in our flesh and not in our spirit... we will fail.&lt;/I&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Huh?? A &quot;spy&quot; of what, for whom?? Only debauched man requires spies. Besides, who needs spies to know the evil that is at work around him. If you&#39;re around the wicked, you&#39;re to be salt and light, not participating in their deeds among them. You&#39;re in the world, but not to be of the world, partakers thereof. Jesus never said to keep the Truth and the way to salvation hidden in your attic and kept secret from the heathen.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;I&gt;as for the church, and those like the mennonites, maybe it is silent because God has told it/them to focus on a different area?&lt;/I&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;I didn&#39;t say the Mennonites were silent, Rick. I instead said that there ain&#39;t many like the Mennonites of &lt;I&gt;that&lt;/I&gt; day that &lt;I&gt;make it known overtly&lt;/I&gt;, albeit even if unintentionally, that they cared nothing about the warmongering president, in that day Woodrow Wilson, today it&#39;s George Bush. Translation? They were NOT silent!. Quite the opposite, in fact. Once again, if you are silent (or indifferent) to a policy, it can mean either you support it, or you oppose it depending on the groupthink aspects. The Mennonites made their opposition, in this case, clear by their total &quot;silence&quot; and lack of a ROAR for Wilsonian warmongering and &quot;making the world safe for democracy&quot; mantra that afflicted the commoners of the day.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;I&gt;you know, and i&#39;m not aiming any of this at you, but merely pointing something out, when we know that a storm is coming, focusing on what the everyone else is doing about it is of no consequence. what is of consequence is what God would have us do. yeah, our country is going to hell in a hand basket and it&#39;s run by wicked people.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;........so what? as the ordained piano player should only play the piano, as the ordained guitarist should only play the guitar, i think God&#39;s people should &lt;B&gt;focus on God&#39;s business.&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;...which is the world, the people in it, that is. On this, I agree. Again, James 2:15-16 8).</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115648748069726689'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115648748069726689'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156487460000#c115648748069726689' title=''/><author><name>dixiedog</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/09845646940134894119</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-504942784"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 25, 2006 at 12:31 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115644478379729538</id><published>2006-08-24T12:39:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-24T12:39:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>This story goes along with the Rickoverian Paradox...</title><content type='html'>This story goes along with the Rickoverian Paradox you posted on the Birch Blog.  (This might be a stretch but I&#39;ve been wanting to go back to that one.)One of the things that upsets me is that of high ranking officials attempting to give consolation to those who have lost loved ones in the war by saying they died to protect our freedom.  The sad thing is, if those high officials had done their jobs and taken their oaths to support and defend the Constitution against all enemies, foreign and domestic seriously, that death would not have occurred...at least not at that time and place.  &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Whose job is it to force our government to obey the Constitution?  The Congress - they have shown they are complicit in giving the Executive Branch anything it wants?  The Supreme Court - it is too busy with its own agenda of making up rulings (Kelo) and not looking at others (Daniel New).  The military - it is too busy trying to find relevance in a post USSR world to think about its oath, and besides, no one ever told them that their Commander In Chief might be the one destroying the document they are sworn to defend and what to do to stop it.  The States - they are no longer represented at the federal level.  The people - they are convinced that a vote for a third party is a vote for the bad guy (whichever party) and so the choice is tweedle dee or tweedle dum.  &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Probably the scariest part is that even if the government toppled tomorrow, there appear to be no leaders of the Founding Fathers&#39; caliber to take over.  Nature abhors a vacuum.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115644478379729538'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115644478379729538'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156444740000#c115644478379729538' title=''/><author><name>Neo</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/08839164398247281003</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1580334153"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 24, 2006 at 12:39 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115643092276690777</id><published>2006-08-24T08:48:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-24T08:48:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>These stories are scary. The people who are reacti...</title><content type='html'>These stories are scary. The people who are reacting with such harsh opposition to an upside down flag are just the type of people who will do the governments bidding when it comes to enforcing a &quot;Police State&quot;. An American can&#39;t display an upside down US flag in protest to the war without repercussions, but an &quot;Illegal Immigrant&quot; can display an upside down US flag in a public protest and that&#39;s no problem. What has happened in this country that would allow things like this to take place?</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115643092276690777'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115643092276690777'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156430880000#c115643092276690777' title=''/><author><name>DJS</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/03616609130163676140</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1644214747"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 24, 2006 at 8:48 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115640903954784107</id><published>2006-08-24T02:43:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-24T02:43:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>it seems that our flag has become a golden calf.  ...</title><content type='html'>it seems that our flag has become a golden calf.  &quot;it&#39;s a god that should be reveered (spl) and curse those who should want to bring down what it represents.&quot;  the problem is that the flag represents different things to different people.  it&#39;s amazing that those who wish america to be be free, truly wish that it is only free for them and those who share their idealogy.  to be honest, these folks have the same mindset as the terrorists--&quot;follow our religion (convert) or be destroyed&quot;.  morons.  why are people so bold on the net, yet would not for the life of themselves, carry out their threat...by themselves...in the flesh?  heh.  that man who flew his flag updside down has more courage than them all.  truth be told, given the state of our nation, all flags should be flown upside down.   ......but that&#39;s just me.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;and to dixiedog, it may be a good thing that some do not speak out against the horrors that are going on.  hear me out.  God has given everyone a purpose.  each person is to walk in his purpose and accomplish it.  to fail to do so would be to get to heaven and to hear....,&quot;I never knew you.&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;i seriously believe that, although the Lord does care about what&#39;s going on down here, He is not worried about it cuz He&#39;s got it under control.  His message to the church right now may not be to focus on what our govt is doing because there are greater issues He needs to address in His church.  i mean, if His church is focused on the affairs of this world, then how can it be effective spiritually if it&#39;s paying attention to man and not to God? &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;john the baptist had a mission--make way the coming of the Lord.  now, along the way john got into doing something else...telling king herod he was wrong.  herod was wrong, but what did God tell john to do?  &quot;make way the coming of the Lord.&quot;  what was his focus to be?  God would send nathan to rebuke king david without many present, or in private, but john?  john railed against herod in public.  do we aever read &quot;and God sent john to see herod&quot;?  nope.  john got distracted from his focus/mission, and john got his head lopped off.  when you think about it, had john not attacked herod, he may have become an apostle...but....he spoke to an issue that was not his purpose....and died because of it.  (maybe i&#39;m wrong, but go tell the president at the white house gates he&#39;s x, y, and z and see what happens...hard to be affective for Christ behind bars).  but i digress.  back to my point.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;esther.  esther had a purpose, one single purpose.  save her people.  had she done anything else the jews might have been wiped out.  but of course that would not have happened because of God&#39;s promise, but things would have been in a bind.  back to esther.  &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;ESTHER HAD TO KEEP HER MOUTH SHUT.  satan knew God would try to save His people but did not know how He would do it.  satan was expecting God to move one way, but did not see that He would sneak a jewess into the kings harem and have this jewess becaome his wife only so at the right moment, she would speak up to influence the king&#39;s decision.  i&#39;m sure satan thought God was gonna replace the king or something.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;so what am i saying?  God has spies.  and spies (like us) do not/should not reveal themselves until it&#39;s time to move or act.  some groups may be quiet out of fear, but there are some, i am sure, that are spies, and are accomplishing a mission, that in the end, will change things.  we want to see changes one way.  and that &quot;way&quot; is what satan may be focused on and trying to prevent...and doing a good job at preventing.  so God says, &quot;ok, i see you satan...and what you are doing.  but while you are looking that way, I will move in these ways.&quot;  it&#39;s not hard for God to trick satan.  He did it at calvary.  so if we are working in our flesh and not in our spirit... we will fail.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;as for the church, and those like the mennonites, maybe it is silent because God has told it/them to focus on a different area?&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;you know, and i&#39;m not aiming any of this at you, but merely pointing something out, when we know that a storm is coming, focusing on what the everyone else is doing about it is of no consequence.  what is of consequence is what God would have us do.  yeah, our country is going to hell in a hand basket and it&#39;s run by wicked people.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;........so what?  as the ordained piano player should only play the piano, as the ordained guitarist should only play the guitar, i think God&#39;s people should focus on God&#39;s business.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;now, if God&#39;s business is for a person to deal with the current mess in our govt?  cool.  that&#39;s his puropse, and God&#39;s annointing will go with him.  we know what we know for a reason.  we can prepare for what&#39;s beyond the horizon.  we will have to prepare for those who are coming because when we&#39;re gone, God&#39;s plan will still go forth, and those &quot;left behind&quot; will have nothing unless we leave it to them.  so in the immortal words of my sister....&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&quot;hello, i was your grandfather.  just in case you were a complete idiot and did nothing to prepare for the current mess your country, and you, are now in...you know, not even the Holy Ghost is left?...then you may find these weapons and items at this location.&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;to everything there is a season.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115640903954784107'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115640903954784107'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156408980000#c115640903954784107' title=''/><author><name>rick</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/12473173027048173880</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-870704727"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 24, 2006 at 2:43 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115640537981019627</id><published>2006-08-24T01:42:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2006-08-24T01:42:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>I agree. That&#39;s surely a sad and tragic prima faci...</title><content type='html'>I agree. That&#39;s surely a sad and tragic prima facie exposé of what a warrior mentality, conjured and brewed up by a government-media complex, produces in &lt;I&gt;any&lt;/I&gt; age. However, I&#39;d caveat that and say that in the current age there ain&#39;t many, like those Mennonites and others at that time, who loudly or otherwise overtly oppose the imperial warmongering undertaken by whatever contemporary regime in office at the time.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Deafening silence or indifference is as much a show of popular support for a given warmongering duopolistic regime as the loud roar of a &quot;conservative&quot; or liberal commentariat.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;BTW, I noticed you &lt;I&gt;seriously&lt;/I&gt; dig posting images, as if it was a newfound capability you recently discovered with this blog ;). But please, don&#39;t take offense. By all means, keep &#39;em coming; I&#39;m just making note of it is all.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115640537981019627'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115636719773741673/comments/default/115640537981019627'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html?showComment=1156405320000#c115640537981019627' title=''/><author><name>dixiedog</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/09845646940134894119</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/madness-that-is-war-patriotism.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115636719773741673' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115636719773741673' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-504942784"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="August 24, 2006 at 1:42 AM"/></entry></feed>